WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.594
Host: Orient the two nerves at the lung root
and connect one to its main motor

2
00:00:04.594 --> 00:00:06.053
Host: target.

3
00:00:06.053 --> 00:00:11.981
Guide: The phrenic nerve runs anterior to the
lung root and supplies the diaphragm through
fibres

4
00:00:11.981 --> 00:00:20.274
Guide: principally from C3–C5. The vagus runs
posterior to the root and contributes to
thoracic autonomic

5
00:00:20.274 --> 00:00:22.034
Guide: networks.

6
00:00:22.034 --> 00:00:26.153
Host: A diagram places the diaphragm low in
the thorax.

7
00:00:26.153 --> 00:00:29.982
Host: Why does this not imply thoracic motor
roots?

8
00:00:29.982 --> 00:00:34.805
Guide: Its phrenic motor supply principally
comes from C3–C5.

9
00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:41.024
Guide: Adult position and developmental
history must be distinguished from segmental
motor supply.
